<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 492)</h2>
<p><b>Optimized media plays properly the first time through.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: optimized media got no read-ahead at all.</b> Every frame was decoded the moment it was needed, by seeking the movie and decoding forward from the nearest keyframe — so the first pass through a shot stuttered or showed nothing, and only the second was smooth, off the cache. Switching shots mid-playback did it again each time.</li>
<li>The cause: a stand-in is wrapped so it can report the original's frame numbers, and the read-ahead identified movies by their outermost type — so it never recognised one, and quietly did nothing. It asks the source what it is now.</li>
<li>Measured on a 290-frame stand-in: a first pass went from <b>289 late frames to 0</b>. Jumping to an unplayed shot during playback went from every frame to 13, which is the reader starting up — under a second.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
