<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 490)</h2>
<p><b>Quitting knows what you have actually saved.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: the quit prompt appeared after you had just saved, and choosing Save didn't quit.</b> The comparison that decides whether anything is unsaved was being made between two different snapshots of the app's state, so once you changed anything at all it never agreed with itself again — the session read as unsaved forever, and Save could never satisfy it. Only Don't Save got you out. It is now computed from the session itself, so both sides of the comparison are the same thing.</li>
<li><b>Fixed: moving between clips counted as an unsaved change.</b> Saving stamps the current shot with the live loop range and rate, so simply changing shot moved that stamp and looked like an edit. Only your actual work — color spaces, grades, marks, notes, trims — counts now.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
